                <pb facs="1053" n="917" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg917"/>

                <head>No. 655.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 30,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 122.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 199 of 1st instant, in reference to the appropriation of the Haytian
                    Government of $250,000 to relieve the victims of the late fires, and discussing
                    the general responsibility of the Government in this regard. The subject will
                    have due consideration, if any case should be presented for the decision of this
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
